{
 "_about": "The four holes, in the order a round plays them. Every length is in centimetres on the ground, x to the right of the tee and z toward it (the lotus is at negative z). bounds: x0, z0, x1, z1 (outside is out of bounds). base: the ground's height before shapes; rough: the amplitude and scale of a seeded unevenness. hazard: [kind, level] where kind is water or lava. hills and plateaus: [x, z, radius, height] (a negative height is a hollow); ridges: [x0, z0, x1, z1, radius, height] along a line (a negative height is a channel). fairways: [x0, z0, x1, z1, width], mown in stripes. paints: a theme paint along a line of a width. pads: lily pads [x, z, radius] on the water or ground. webs: [x, z, height above the ground, radius, kick x, kick z in cm/s]. mushrooms: [x, z]. items: [jump or wings, x, z], floating. shot_flies: flies along the arc a shot flies, from a point toward another at a power in percent, how many. flies: lines [x0, z0, x1, z1, how many, height, and optionally how much higher the middle rises]. props: placed scenery, the larger ones solid. scatter: scenery placed by a seeded roll inside a region away from play, or round the hole outside it when no region is given. buildings: [x0, z0, x1, z1, height]. lanes: cars along z between two x at a speed in cm/s.",
